# Bash local declarations

## Invalid (breaks at runtime)

Do not put `-a`, `-A`, `-i`, or `-n` after scalar names. Bash treats the flag as a variable name:

```bash
# BAD
local profile script -a args=()
local mode="$1" -a items=()

# GOOD
local profile script
local -a args=()
local mode="$1"
local -a items=()
```

## Arrays

- Declare arrays on their own `local -a` line (or `local -A` for associative).
- Scalars and arrays can be separate lines in the same function.
- `local pkg missing=()` is OK (implicit array for `missing` in bash 4+), but prefer `local -a missing=()` for clarity.

## Empty array command prefixes

Safe pattern when a command prefix may be empty:

```bash
local -a env_args=()
# ...
"${env_args[@]}" bash "$script" "${args[@]}"
```

Requires bash 4.4+ with `set -u` (our scripts use bash 4+).
